  "title": "The state of consciousness never comes apart from its contents",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "0518bc10-3700-4a6c-87db-5f72d7d88d3c",
      "text": "One cannot be conscious of a taste while in an unconscious state, and a healthy subject cannot be in a conscious state while conscious of nothing. State and contents form one whole, and studying one without the other gives half an answer.",
